WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.572
On this slide, we are focusing on convert text into numbers.

00:00:04.572 --> 00:00:10.072
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:10.072 --> 00:00:16.377
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:16.377 --> 00:00:18.017
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:25.662
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:25.662 --> 00:00:26.992
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:32.397
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.

00:00:32.397 --> 00:00:37.357
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:40.752
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:47.452
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:47.452 --> 00:00:49.861
from the names and output.
